dialogue cohesion_barbarian_engineer
title: Hit it there
trigger: Cohesion barbarian engineer level=2
once
speaker commander $commander
speaker barbarian barbarian
speaker engineer engineer

node open commander
  The Engineer has a smashed Halcyon housing in pieces on a cloth, fitting the shards together. The Barbarian, who smashed it, is eating a cold potato and pretending not to watch.
  -> whole

node whole engineer
  This was a seal housing. Halcyon. Older than the Choir, possibly older than the road. I had seven questions for it. Now I've got a puzzle with no corners.
  -> shooting

node shooting barbarian
  It was shooting at the Cleric. Things that shoot at the Cleric get hit. That's my whole list of questions.
  -> there

node there engineer
  I'm not saying don't hit it. I'm saying hit it there, on the collar, not in the middle where the good parts are. Is that so much to ask?
  * The Engineer calls the spot, the Barbarian hits it. That's a plan. -> called
    do: AddCohesion barbarian engineer 10
    do: SetFlag barbarian_engineer:fight_called
  * In a fight, the Barbarian doesn't stop to take notes. Neither should you. -> notes
    do: AddCohesion barbarian engineer -4
    do: AddTrust engineer -3
    do: SetFlag barbarian_engineer:fight_notes
  * Argue this before the fight, both of you, not after. -> before
    do: AddCohesion barbarian engineer 6
    do: SetFlag barbarian_engineer:fight_before
  * Learn the word. Saltmoss. If the red's up and you need a spot hit, shout that first. -> word
    if: FlagSet barbarian:rage_word
    do: AddCohesion barbarian engineer 10
    do: AddTrust barbarian 2
    do: SetFlag barbarian_engineer:fight_word

node called barbarian
  You shout, I swing. Aye. Shout loud. And don't shout "collar". I don't know which end's the collar.
  -> redline

node notes engineer
  Notes are how I keep the lights on, Commander. Fine. I'll take them after. From the bits.
  -> redline

node before barbarian
  Before. Over supper. With drawings, I suppose. Go on, then. Draw me a collar.
  -> redline

node word engineer
  Saltmoss, then "collar". I'm writing that down. Page forty. You're on page forty now, Barbarian, with the good questions.
  -> redline

node redline barbarian
  Somebody back home wants you square, I hear. When we get near your old city, I stand behind you. Close enough to be seen.
  * We said the crew pays the debt together. The Barbarian's crew. -> together
    if: FlagSet engineer:debt_shared
    do: AddCohesion barbarian engineer 10
    do: SetFlag barbarian_engineer:redline_together
  * Redline gets nothing. Let them see the Barbarian and do the sum. -> stare
    if: FlagSet engineer:debt_defied
    do: AddCohesion barbarian engineer 8
    do: SetFlag barbarian_engineer:redline_stare
  * No fists in the Underspire. That's an order. -> order
    do: AddCohesion barbarian engineer 4
    do: AddTrust barbarian -3
    do: SetFlag barbarian_engineer:redline_order
  * Behind, then. Not in front. It's the Engineer's debt to close. -> behind
    do: AddCohesion barbarian engineer 6
    do: SetFlag barbarian_engineer:redline_behind

node together engineer
  Together. Redline sends letters on red wire and counts in fish. I'd like to see the sum when a whole crew walks in, and this one at the back.
  -> close

node stare engineer
  Do the sum. Ha. Redline's good at sums. They'll get to the Barbarian and stop counting.
  -> close

node order barbarian
  No fists. I heard. I'll stand there with my hands in my pockets and look at them, then. Nobody ever ordered me not to look.
  -> close

node behind engineer
  My debt to close. Yes. But it's a lot easier to close with somebody standing where they can see you. Thank you, Barbarian.
  -> close

node close commander
  The Engineer pushes a shard across the cloth. The Barbarian picks it up, turns it the wrong way, then the right way, and it fits.
